    "narrative": "With the June 11th slate offering limited opportunities, our focus shifts to maximizing marginal gains. **Geraldo Perdomo** stands as our strongest play of the day with a 56.04 efficiency score. Despite the scarcity of elite production, **Geraldo Perdomo** benefits from a favorable matchup against Phillips (xERA 4.33), and his placement in the #5 hole provides enough volume to justify the start in our current configuration. **Taylor Ward** follows closely at 52.71; while he faces a stiffer test against the arm of Woo, the significant park factors in his favor buoy his projection, keeping him firmly in the OF1 slot. \n\nWe are navigating a thinning roster due to the unfortunate status of **Cal Raleigh** and **Yainer Diaz**, both currently sidelined on the IL. This has forced **Masyn Winn** (50.76) and **Gleyber Torres** (48.51) into the lineup as our primary MI/2B options. **Masyn Winn** remains a vital component of our strategy given his sprint speed\u2014a commodity we cannot afford to bench in this league\u2014even though the matchup against Scott presents a neutral profile. **Gleyber Torres** is being started despite a negative adjustment for the dynamic platoon disadvantage against Matthews, as we lack a superior alternative on the bench today.\n\nThe most notable bench decision involved our assessment of depth versus the high-floor requirements of a 5x5 Roto format. While players like **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Lawrence Butler** are held back by scheduled team off-days, we are closely monitoring the utilization of our utility bench. No depth piece effectively challenged the starting four today, as we are prioritizing the volume of **Masyn Winn** and **Geraldo Perdomo** to chip away at the SB and R categories. With no high-impact weather threats currently on the radar, the primary risk remains the high-level efficiency of opposing arms like Woo, which could suppress our team-wide AVG if the middle of our order fails to capitalize on their limited opportunities.",
